orrection in agentic user simulation. The two uncontroversial findings anchoring this are the completion collapse in FM1 at 7B (a 72.8% drop that's large enough to not require confidence intervals) and the scale-dependent severity pattern where 7B shows catastrophic failure while 14B is immune but still miscalibrated.\n\nFM4's reversal becomes a secondary finding emphasizing directional consistency across 10 out of 12 cases rather than effect magnitude, while FM2 and FM3 get folded into a broader discussion of how BCP perturbations produce unpredictable side effects. I'm renaming this to \"Calibration Considered Harmful? Evidence That Behavioral Correction Fails Across Scales in LLM User Simulation\" and positioning it as an empirical warning paper for Findings rather than a taxonomy contribution. Now I need to write the LaTeX paper while being meticulous about data accuracy—every number has to be verified.\n\nLooking at the key metrics: FM1 shows a devastating 72.8% completion drop for AAVE speakers (0.100 vs 0.368 baseline), with multi-run retention at 35.1% for AAVE and 44.5% for Indian speakers, and the bootstrap confidence interval of [-82, -55]% excludes zero. The scale effect is stark—7B models hit 36.8% completion while 14B reaches 61.6%, a 67% relative improvement. At 14B, H3 passes all 4 tests but H2 only passes 1 out of 4. FM4 shows directional alignment in 10 of 12 cases with a mean gap reversal of 17 percentage points and a confidence interval spanning [-3, 37]pp, where AAVE gaps shift from -0.091 to +0.064 and Indian gaps from -0.099 to +0.063 after DPO training.\n\nNow I'm looking at the additional results: FM3 rebounds with a mean improvement of 7.2 percentage points and a confidence interval of [-2.0, 16.5]pp, with all 4 directional tests passing under DPO plus BCP, while FM2 shows a concerning -15.8% mean drop on non-target populations with high variance, and the H2 gap reduction confidence interval of [12, 28]% stays below the 30% threshold.\n\nI'm ready to write the paper now, structuring it to tell the narrative arc of these findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13373,"cache_read_input_tokens":23305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13373},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"343f4365-21a5-4930-9644-67113182a5fa","uuid":"e3713926-c338-460a-93ac-72f28ac14203"}
